  "memo": "Walt Disney Co. (DIS) has navigated macroeconomic headwinds, resulting in a challenging but improving bottom line over the past two fiscal years. In fiscal year 2023, the company generated $87.0 billion in total revenue, reflecting modest top-line growth. Operating income reached $15.9 billion, while adjusted net income was $6.8 billion, yielding GAAP earnings per share of $1.57. Free cash flow came in at $9.2 billion. Fiscal year 2024 proved tougher, with total revenue declining slightly to $86.8 billion. Despite softer top-line performance, free cash flow improved significantly to $10.5 billion, driven by disciplined capital allocation. However, profitability metrics deteriorated, with adjusted operating income falling to $14.6 billion and adjusted net income dropping to $5.3 billion, leading to GAAP EPS declining to $1.10. The core theme park and experiences segment emerged as the primary growth driver, offsetting declines in media and entertainment. Management remains focused on executing its turnaround strategy, balancing cost cuts with investment in high-demand parks. We see DIS as a turnaround play with strong cash generation, trading at a premium to historical averages despite near-term margin headwinds."
